{
    "_note": "Recurring-series programming for Maker Channel (see channels/publish.php). This channel's airtime is a 12-hour, 12-show repeating lineup -- twelve real YouTube imports, each editorially approved up to an 18-episode cap (see each series/<id>/series.json), each given one fixed 60-minute daily slot plus a second slot exactly 12 hours later, so the same ordered lineup plays twice every calendar day (wall-to-wall, no gaps), mirroring Science & Engineering's proven lineup shape. Every block opts into multi-episode packing (packing.enabled, mode sequential, on_unfit defer, minimum_remaining 30s) so a one-hour slot plays as many complete episodes as actually fit (most of this catalog's approved episodes run 10-30 minutes) instead of exactly one. boundary.mode is hard on every block: the longest approved episode across the whole catalog is 3596s (Jeremy Fielding's 'Engineer Vs Bee - Round 1'), under the 3600s slot, so no block has ever actually needed to run over -- the handful of episodes that would have exceeded the slot (my mechanics' 3636s/10868s outliers; Clickspring's 4198s 'Chill Out Extended Cut') were left unapproved specifically so every block can stay hard, matching Science & Engineering's own documented posture. Deliberately excludes stuff-made-here (already Science's flagship, reused here would blur Maker's own distinct lineup) even though the architecture fully supports it, independently rotated, if a future editor wants to add it.",
